1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 {... "A Giuoco Piano. Both sides having castled early, Black advanced his KRP and KKtP to release the pinned K Kt, when White sacrificed the knight for two pawns, but did not continue energetically enough to recover the piece, or get a compensating attack. Black brought his king into safety, and won with the extra piece." Source: The Field, 4 May 1907} 0-1

